{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"e631ef91-5c10-49e8-83ea-941f20525f16","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"keepass\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-001\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"KeePass must be downloaded and installed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying who performs the download and installation, and omits target platform, version, or source preconditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"has no limits in length. A whole sentence can be used with more than 100 characters.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses illustrative weak phrasing ('can be used') and leaves unclear whether 'no limits in length' permits an empty (0-character) password.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflates a 'Folder' with a .kdb file, uses unclear syntax ('type the database can read', 'and that is'), and leaves unclear whether '“name”.kdb' denotes any filename with a .kdb extension or a literal name.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify who selects the target or how the system handles selection of an unsupported or unreadable file.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains unclear referents ('the previews [previous] one', 'if selected'—for creation, saving, or opening?) and does not define uniqueness scope (same directory vs. globally, case sensitivity).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Fails to specify the directory/scope of name uniqueness and whether user confirmation or a warning is required before overwriting an existing database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Unclear whether 'them' refers to all entries in the database or only selected/filtered entries, and whether plural 'entries' requires more than one entry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior (e.g., disabled print option or error message) when printing is attempted on an empty database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'All data related to the word' is vague regarding which fields are searched, matching criteria (case sensitivity, substring vs. whole word), and whether sensitive fields like passwords are shown in plaintext.\"\n    },\n    {\n      